{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q018_tal_effector_repeat_lengths\",\"answer\":\"In public SCOPe release 2.08, all three domains are explicitly classified in family a.298.1.1, “TAL (transcription activator-like) effector,” within superfamily a.298.1 (“TAL effector-like”), fold a.298 (“Left-handed alpha-alpha superhelix”), and class a (“All alpha proteins”). Their unequal lengths—d2kq5a_ (PthA), 51 residues; d3v6pa_ (dHax3), 373 residues; and d4cj9a_ (BurrH), 752 residues—reflect different numbers of tandem, homologous TAL repeat units, not different fold or family identities. SCOPe explicitly labels d2kq5a_ “single repeat” and flags d2kq5a_ and d3v6pa_ with the repeat-number inconsistency code “re,” defined for family domains composed of different numbers of small repeating units. The family’s canonical representative repeat is the 34-residue segment 4cj9 A:259–292. Thus, family membership captures close evolutionary/structural relatedness of the repeated module and its characteristic superhelical assembly; it does not require comparable full-domain length. The three records are distinct proteins and organisms, so the shared family assignment alone does not justify transferring exact repeat counts, residue boundaries, DNA-target specificity, or detailed biological function. Likewise, 4cj9 A:259–292 is a canonical representative coordinate range, not a boundary mapping for d2kq5a_ or d3v6pa_; using it as a structural template requires repeat-level alignment and independent sequence/structure evidence rather than whole-chain length matching.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info — /api/v1/; /api/v1/releases/current\",\"mcp__scope__get_scop_domains — /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/annotations\",\"mcp__scope__get_scop_sequence — /api/v1/sequences/sids/d2kq5a_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json; /api/v1/sequences/sids/d3v6pa_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json; /api/v1/sequences/sids/d4cj9a_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json\"]}]}"}}
